  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A Hausdorff topological group G is called minimal if it does not admit a strictly coarser Hausdorff group topology. A topological group is called Raikov complete if its two-sided uniform structure is complete. Is it true that an arbitrary Cartesian product of Raikov complete minimal topological groups remains minimal?",
